# Variables passed to the eval sandbox, where the LTC checks of every project run.
# Copy to docker/eval.env (git-ignored) and recreate the stack: ./rebuild.sh
#
# From the sandbox your machine is host.containers.internal, not localhost.
# Names containing TOKEN, SECRET, PASSWORD, API_KEY, CREDENTIAL... are refused: the sandbox
# never holds credentials.
#
# Test databases: CLike creates a disposable database per project and REQ (recreated at every
# eval) on this server, for every LTC variable with "provision": "postgres_database" (and for
# *DATABASE_URL variables described as PostgreSQL). Local PostgreSQL with trust auth, a user
# that may create databases:
# CLIKE_EVAL_POSTGRES_URL=postgresql://me@host.containers.internal:5432/postgres
#
# Values only you have ("provision": "external" in the LTC), e.g.:
# PROVIDER_SANDBOX_URL=https://sandbox.provider.example
#
# A value set here always wins over what CLike would provision, e.g. a fixed database:
# APP_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://me@host.containers.internal:5432/app_test
